2026-10-11 11:34:00,059 - RapidOCR - INFO: [[[[1177.0, 95.0], [1353.0, 95.0], [1353.0, 121.0], [1177.0, 121.0]], 'BiBTrialProtocol', 0.9963232763111591], [[[881.0, 124.0], [1352.0, 127.0], [1352.0, 153.0], [880.0, 150.0]], 'VersionDate:June9,2022;September8,2023', 0.983277573397285], [[[180.0, 198.0], [1343.0, 195.0], [1343.0, 228.0], [180.0, 231.0]], 'gently mixed (not shaken) by inverting the syringe, and the surfactant or surfactant + budesonide', 0.9960504229535762], [[[180.0, 233.0], [1320.0, 233.0], [1320.0, 262.0], [180.0, 262.0]], 'mixture will be administered in a manner similar to that of routine surfactant therapy. Once the', 0.9823843420793613], [[[181.0, 266.0], [1264.0, 266.0], [1264.0, 295.0], [181.0, 295.0]], 'kit is spent, all masked contents of the kit will be returned to the kit, which is resealed and', 0.9872256002928081], [[[178.0, 300.0], [1319.0, 299.0], [1319.0, 332.0], [178.0, 333.0]], 'returned to pharmacy for end processing. The randomization ID tied to a kit does not include a', 0.9925198821311302], [[[180.0, 336.0], [581.0, 338.0], [581.0, 368.0], [180.0, 366.0]], 'coded randomization assignment.', 0.9959551961191239], [[[181.0, 399.0], [1341.0, 398.0], [1341.0, 431.0], [181.0, 432.0]], 'Additional logistical discussion of the masking process is discussed in the Manual of Operations.', 0.9948609969050614], [[[180.0, 464.0], [817.0, 466.0], [817.0, 496.0], [180.0, 494.0]], '4.2.6. Control or Monitoring of Co-interventions', 0.9972270602981249], [[[179.0, 512.0], [1332.0, 511.0], [1332.0, 547.0], [179.0, 548.0]], 'Early (< 7 days after the last dose of study drug) postnatal systemic steroids will be discouraged', 0.9926958442950735], [[[179.0, 548.0], [1313.0, 547.0], [1313.0, 580.0], [179.0, 581.0]], 'and reserved only for infants (at clinician discretion) who have fluid-resistant hypotension OR', 0.9964889156190972], [[[180.0, 585.0], [1245.0, 582.0], [1245.0, 612.0], [180.0, 615.0]], 'vasopressor-resistant hypotension, OR evidence of hyponatremia and low serum cortisol', 0.9921593034968657], [[[179.0, 617.0], [1251.0, 615.0], [1251.0, 648.0], [179.0, 650.0]], 'concentrations (as per local NICU definitions, with suggested definitions including: fluid', 0.994289552503162], [[[179.0, 653.0], [1330.0, 652.0], [1330.0, 682.0], [179.0, 683.0]], 'resistant hypotension defined as receiving 20 ml/kg or more of fluid infusion for hypotension in', 0.9895280531297127], [[[178.0, 686.0], [1291.0, 685.0], [1291.0, 718.0], [178.0, 719.0]], '< 2 hours; vasopressor resistant hypotension defined as receipt of treatment with at least one', 0.9958331863930885], [[[181.0, 724.0], [1078.0, 724.0], [1078.0, 753.0], [181.0, 753.0]], 'vasopressor at a higher dose such as dopamine at 10 mcg/kg/min or more).', 0.9879257621036636], [[[180.0, 785.0], [1348.0, 785.0], [1348.0, 817.0], [180.0, 817.0]], 'The use of postnatal steroids at later time points will be considered a secondary outcome and it is', 0.9941247779913623], [[[180.0, 822.0], [1288.0, 819.0], [1288.0, 849.0], [180.0, 852.0]], 'suggested that use of postnatal systemic steroids not exceed the dosing used in DART or the', 0.9878710652445699], [[[180.0, 854.0], [1298.0, 854.0], [1298.0, 887.0], [180.0, 887.0]], 'Hydrocortisone trial (if hydrocortisone is used), except in patients with demonstrated adrenal', 0.9938473695136131], [[[178.0, 888.0], [347.0, 890.0], [346.0, 923.0], [177.0, 921.0]], 'insufficiency.', 0.9899919458798], [[[178.0, 952.0], [1228.0, 953.0], [1228.0, 986.0], [178.0, 985.0]], 'Other co-interventions (e.g. use of ibuprofen or other agents for PDA management) are', 0.9968068178962258], [[[178.0, 988.0], [1323.0, 986.0], [1323.0, 1018.0], [178.0, 1020.0]], 'permissible as per clinician preference or unit practice, although such use would be recorded in', 0.9870052815725406], [[[179.0, 1022.0], [1328.0, 1022.0], [1328.0, 1055.0], [179.0, 1055.0]], 'this pragmatic trial. However, prophylactic or therapeutic use of indomethacin during the seven', 0.9942260635526556], [[[180.0, 1057.0], [1353.0, 1057.0], [1353.0, 1089.0], [180.0, 1089.0]], 'days following the last dose of study drug is not permissible in this study due to the possibility of', 0.9830364248540142], [[[180.0, 1091.0], [1195.0, 1091.0], [1195.0, 1121.0], [180.0, 1121.0]], 'increased risk for SIP. All reportable, concomitant medications will be collected and', 0.9816626871333403], [[[179.0, 1127.0], [334.0, 1125.0], [335.0, 1155.0], [180.0, 1157.0]], 'summarized.', 0.9997005679390647], [[[180.0, 1190.0], [1257.0, 1192.0], [1257.0, 1222.0], [180.0, 1220.0]], 'A comprehensive safety and efficacy evaluation will be performed for this trial, including', 0.9853097193770939], [[[181.0, 1226.0], [1220.0, 1226.0], [1220.0, 1254.0], [181.0, 1254.0]], 'outcomes listed below in Sections 4.2.7 - 4.2.10. All safety variables will be evaluated', 0.9805860946124251], [[[179.0, 1259.0], [1286.0, 1256.0], [1286.0, 1289.0], [179.0, 1292.0]], 'prospectively. The enrolled infants are extremely premature infants admitted to the neonatal', 0.9993356764316559], [[[179.0, 1295.0], [1268.0, 1293.0], [1268.0, 1323.0], [179.0, 1325.0]], 'intensive care unit, and are routinely monitored by a team of highly trained physicians and', 0.9979911459671272], [[[178.0, 1327.0], [1326.0, 1329.0], [1326.0, 1361.0], [178.0, 1359.0]], 'nursing staff, usually with continuous monitoring of heart rate, pulse oximetry, respiratory rate,', 0.9927344747952053], [[[178.0, 1363.0], [1316.0, 1361.0], [1316.0, 1394.0], [178.0, 1396.0]], 'temperature, and other vital signs at frequent intervals. The safety parameters being monitored', 0.9982529307666578], [[[181.0, 1398.0], [1249.0, 1398.0], [1249.0, 1428.0], [181.0, 1428.0]], 'are part of the routine clinical monitoring in all participating NICUs (standard of care for', 0.9928211835415467], [[[180.0, 1433.0], [474.0, 1433.0], [474.0, 1463.0], [180.0, 1463.0]], 'neonatal intensive care).', 0.9881400299072266], [[[180.0, 1496.0], [502.0, 1498.0], [502.0, 1528.0], [180.0, 1526.0]], '4.2.7. Primary Outcome', 0.9804273518649015], [[[181.0, 1547.0], [1257.0, 1547.0], [1257.0, 1577.0], [181.0, 1577.0]], "The primary outcome is physiologic BPD or death by 36 weeks' post-menstrual age in all", 0.9853678986776707], [[[180.0, 1582.0], [1275.0, 1582.0], [1275.0, 1612.0], [180.0, 1612.0]], 'randomized extremely preterm infants and will be recorded by the Research Coordinator at', 0.9923081899231131], [[[180.0, 1618.0], [777.0, 1618.0], [777.0, 1648.0], [180.0, 1648.0]], 'participating centers, using existing GDB criteria.', 0.9899189986434638], [[[180.0, 1680.0], [542.0, 1682.0], [542.0, 1712.0], [180.0, 1709.0]], '4.2.8. Secondary Outcomes', 0.9844977474212646], [[[178.0, 1727.0], [1278.0, 1728.0], [1278.0, 1763.0], [178.0, 1762.0]], 'The following secondary outcomes will be assessed for all randomized subjects, with many', 0.9941741038452495], [[[181.0, 1764.0], [512.0, 1764.0], [512.0, 1794.0], [181.0, 1794.0]], 'being standard in the NRN:', 0.9972719366733844], [[[746.0, 1860.0], [785.0, 1860.0], [785.0, 1892.0], [746.0, 1892.0]], '20', 0.9998396337032318]]
